{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_1","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/zsh -lc \"rg -n 'initial-holder|\"'^'\"\\\\(defn .*holder|\"'^'\"\\\\(defn holding|\"'^'\"\\\\(defn observe-grant|\"'^'\"\\\\(defn.*renew|\"'^'\"\\\\(defn at-bound|\"'^'\"\\\\(deftest.*holder|H1|H2|H3|H4|H5|S5|\"'^## 5|''^## 6'\"' src/cljc/dao/lease.cljc test/dao/lease_test.cljc docs/design/dao.lease.implementation-plan.md; rg --files collab | rg 'lease.*p3|lease.*holder'\"","aggregated_output":"docs/design/dao.lease.implementation-plan.md:170:| H1 | A holder observes its grant before acting and establishes the grantor authored it by the composition's attribution; a holder that has not observed a grantor-authored grant holds nothing, and a forged/non-grantor `:accepted` establishes nothing | `[D]` *The holder* |\ndocs/design/dao.lease.implementation-plan.md:171:| H2 | A holder renews at **strictly less than half** the duration, measured against ticks on its own tick stream; a renewal is an append returning `:dao.stream/ok`, and any other outcome does not advance the holder's bound. The holder's renewal interval is a composition value strictly below half the duration, so a successful next renewal is guaranteed before half the duration elapses; an interval at or above half already violates the sizing relation | `[D]` *The holder*, *Sizing* |\ndocs/design/dao.lease.implementation-plan.md:172:| H3 | A holder stops acting at the bound — the earlier of duration since the later of its last renewal and its observed grant, and the cap the grant carries — whether or not anything has been heard | `[D]` *The holder* |\ndocs/design/dao.lease.implementation-plan.md:173:| H4 | A holder releases when done — appending `:released` — and stops its own activity; it does not reclaim and does not author `:lapsed`. The grantor still performs the reclaim and records it | `[D]` *The holder* |\ndocs/design/dao.lease.implementation-plan.md:174:| H5 | The holder's bound bounds attention, not access: a holder needing exclusion obtains it from the resource, not from this vocabulary | `[D]` *The holder* |\ndocs/design/dao.lease.implementation-plan.md:200:| S5 | The holder's renewal interval plus one period of its tick stream is strictly below half the granted duration: a renewal lands at the first reading at or past the interval, up to one period late (duration 10, interval 4, ticks 0/3/6 renews at 6 > 5), so the before-half guarantee is bought against interval + period. `renewal-interval` validates this when the period is supplied | `[D]` *new* — review round P3-r2 |\ndocs/design/dao.lease.implementation-plan.md:442:- `observe-grant` (H1: gate on having observed a *grantor-authored* grant);\ndocs/design/dao.lease.implementation-plan.md:443:  `renewal-interval` (H2: a composition value strictly below half the duration)\ndocs/design/dao.lease.implementation-plan.md:444:  and `due-to-renew?` (H2: true when the interval since the last\ndocs/design/dao.lease.implementation-plan.md:445:  renewal/observation reaches `renewal-interval`); `at-bound?` (H3: the earlier\ndocs/design/dao.lease.implementation-plan.md:446:  of duration-since-last-activity and the cap); `release` (H4). Each is a pure\ndocs/design/dao.lease.implementation-plan.md:452:1. **Attribution gate** (H1, finding 15): a forged/non-grantor `:accepted`\ndocs/design/dao.lease.implementation-plan.md:455:2. **Strict renewal** (H2, finding 14): `renewal-interval` is strictly below half\ndocs/design/dao.lease.implementation-plan.md:462:   duration-since-last-activity when the cap is absent or larger (H3).\ndocs/design/dao.lease.implementation-plan.md:464:   (H2, finding 20).\ndocs/design/dao.lease.implementation-plan.md:465:5. **Release** (H4, finding 15): a holder that emits `:released` stops its own\ndocs/design/dao.lease.implementation-plan.md:518:## 5. Host matrix\ndocs/design/dao.lease.implementation-plan.md:538:## 6. Boundary — built here, and what is left owing\ndocs/design/dao.lease.implementation-plan.md:575:  invariant (V1–V7, J1–J16, H1–H5, C1–C8, S1–S4), a decision (D1–D7), a phase, or\ndocs/design/dao.lease.implementation-plan.md:599:| 5 | §7 accounting incomplete | Applied — added V6–V7, J12–J16, H5, C7–C8, S1–S4; §6 records the out-of-scope and unresolved items |\ndocs/design/dao.lease.implementation-plan.md:608:| 14 | Renewal rule inverted | Applied — H2 + 4.3 #2 make the interval strictly below half and treat equality as a violation |\ndocs/design/dao.lease.implementation-plan.md:609:| 15 | H1/H4 unproven | Applied — 4.3 #1 (forged grant) and #5 (release emits `:released`, stops, no reclaim) |\nsrc/cljc/dao/lease.cljc:565:(defn renewal\nsrc/cljc/dao/lease.cljc:1536:;; holder's OWN control flow calls: observe the grant before acting (H1),\nsrc/cljc/dao/lease.cljc:1537:;; renew at strictly less than half the duration (H2), stop at the bound\nsrc/cljc/dao/lease.cljc:1538:;; (H3), release when done (H4). Nothing here installs a timer, renews on a\nsrc/cljc/dao/lease.cljc:1545:;; one state per lease. The bound bounds attention, not access (H5): every\nsrc/cljc/dao/lease.cljc:1549:(defn initial-holder\nsrc/cljc/dao/lease.cljc:1565:                     the composition is arranging (H2/S1); validated here\nsrc/cljc/dao/lease.cljc:1623:(defn renewal-interval\nsrc/cljc/dao/lease.cljc:1625:  is sized to (H2 as amended): strictly below HALF the duration -- equality\nsrc/cljc/dao/lease.cljc:1697:  \"The later of the holder's last renewal and its observed grant (H3): the\nsrc/cljc/dao/lease.cljc:1724:(defn observe-grant\nsrc/cljc/dao/lease.cljc:1725:  \"H1: observe the grant before acting. The grant is held only when the\nsrc/cljc/dao/lease.cljc:1785:(defn at-bound?\nsrc/cljc/dao/lease.cljc:1786:  \"H3: true when the holder's reading has reached the bound -- the earlier\nsrc/cljc/dao/lease.cljc:1801:  The bound bounds attention, not access (H5): this answers a question, it revokes nothing.\"\nsrc/cljc/dao/lease.cljc:1819:(defn observe-renewal\nsrc/cljc/dao/lease.cljc:1825:  `:dao.stream/ok` (H2) -- a `full`, `closed` or\nsrc/cljc/dao/lease.cljc:1844:(defn due-to-renew?\nsrc/cljc/dao/lease.cljc:1845:  \"H2: true when the interval since the later of the last renewal and the\nsrc/cljc/dao/lease.cljc:1871:  \"H4, the release discipline: the holder is done. Returns\nsrc/cljc/dao/lease.cljc:1895:(defn holding?\ntest/dao/lease_test.cljc:3:  holder (H1-H5), per the revised implementation plan's Phase 1, Phase 2\ntest/dao/lease_test.cljc:131:(defn- renewal-from\ntest/dao/lease_test.cljc:644:(deftest non-holder-renewal-is-not-evidence-test\ntest/dao/lease_test.cljc:686:(deftest holder-release-reclaims-with-release-cause-test\ntest/dao/lease_test.cljc:1747:(deftest r3-two-holders-sharing-a-proposal-id-test\ntest/dao/lease_test.cljc:1785:(deftest r3-grant-drained-then-holder-medium-truncated-test\ntest/dao/lease_test.cljc:1892:;; H1-H5: the holder\ntest/dao/lease_test.cljc:1906:  (lease/initial-holder {:self :holder-a\ntest/dao/lease_test.cljc:1919:(defn- renewed-at\ntest/dao/lease_test.cljc:1933:(deftest initial-holder-rejects-misconfiguration-test\ntest/dao/lease_test.cljc:1938:                 (lease/initial-holder {:grantor :grantor\ntest/dao/lease_test.cljc:1943:                 (lease/initial-holder {:self :holder-a\ntest/dao/lease_test.cljc:1948:                 (lease/initial-holder {:self :holder-a\ntest/dao/lease_test.cljc:1953:                 (lease/initial-holder {:self :holder-a\ntest/dao/lease_test.cljc:1958:                 (lease/initial-holder {:self :holder-a\ntest/dao/lease_test.cljc:1964:                 (lease/initial-holder {:self :holder-a\ntest/dao/lease_test.cljc:1970:      (is (some? (lease/initial-holder {:self :holder-a\ntest/dao/lease_test.cljc:1977:  (testing \"H1: a grantor-authored grant is observed and seeds the basis\"\ntest/dao/lease_test.cljc:1983:  (testing \"H1/finding 15: a forged, non-grantor :accepted establishes nothing\"\ntest/dao/lease_test.cljc:1992:  (testing \"H1: a grant naming another holder is not this holder's grant\"\ntest/dao/lease_test.cljc:2023:  (testing \"H2/finding 14: the interval is strictly below half the duration\"\ntest/dao/lease_test.cljc:2043:  (testing \"H2/finding 14: due at the interval, on the holder's own ticks\"\ntest/dao/lease_test.cljc:2060:  (testing \"H2/finding 20: only a :dao.stream/ok append advances the bound\"\ntest/dao/lease_test.cljc:2079:  (testing \"H4: a stopped holder records no renewal\"\ntest/dao/lease_test.cljc:2090:  (testing \"H3: the duration bound, from the later of the last renewal and the grant\"\ntest/dao/lease_test.cljc:2095:  (testing \"H3: the cap fires even with fresh renewals\"\ntest/dao/lease_test.cljc:2106:  (testing \"H3: the earlier of the two bounds governs\"\ntest/dao/lease_test.cljc:2133:  (testing \"H4/finding 15: stop authors exactly :released and stops the activity\"\ntest/dao/lease_test.cljc:2143:  (testing \"H4: a holder that observed no grant holds nothing to release\"\ntest/dao/lease_test.cljc:2146:  (testing \"H4/finding 15: the grantor still reclaims and records; the holder\ntest/dao/lease_test.cljc:2164:;; H5 -- the bound bounds attention, not access -- is structural and has no\ntest/dao/lease_test.cljc:2253:    (let [holder (lease/initial-holder {:self :holder-a\ntest/dao/lease_test.cljc:2268:    (let [holder (lease/initial-holder {:self :holder-a\ntest/dao/lease_test.cljc:2312:                 (lease/initial-holder {:self :holder-a\ntest/dao/lease_test.cljc:2320:                 (lease/initial-holder {:self :holder-a\ntest/dao/lease_test.cljc:2367:  (testing \"P3/H1: one may-I-act predicate, answered for a reading, failing closed\"\ncollab/1789845300000-reviewer-dao-lease-p3-r3.claude-fable-5-1.findings.md\ncollab/1789845300000-reviewer-dao-lease-p3-r3.prompt.md\ncollab/1789844700000-reviewer-dao-lease-p3-r2.prompt.md\ncollab/1789841731000-storage-engineer-dao-lease-p3.prompt.md\ncollab/1789843700000-reviewer-dao-lease-p3.prompt.md\ncollab/1789845600000-architect-dao-lease-p3-signoff.prompt.md\ncollab/1789843700000-reviewer-dao-lease-p3.claude-fable-5-1.findings.md\ncollab/1789844081000-storage-engineer-dao-lease-p3-r2.prompt.md\n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
